-- Regulation W, 12 CFR 223.2 and 223.3: independent tests.
--
-- This file was written independently from the regulation text (../../source/part223.txt, sections 223.2 and 223.3),
-- BEFORE the encoding was read.  Every expected value below was decided from the words of the
-- regulation alone and then left alone: where a run against the answer-FALSE stubs, or against the
-- real encoding, disagrees with a line, the line is the question, not the answer.
-- The points where the text is genuinely open are collected in independent-readings.md, one entry each (R1 to R16),
-- and every assertion that depends on one of them sits in section `Contested readings` and names its entry.
-- Everything before that section depends on nothing open, except that a few assertions name the `Readings` constructor they use
-- (`step A as` with `chain readings`, which says what that reading must give); each such line says so.
--
-- Conventions.
--   The member bank is always "Bank".  Every voting holding is in the class "Common" unless a second class is the point.
--   A voting holding carries percent of equity capital 0 (so the reason for control is the voting test alone),
--   a nonvoting equity holding carries percent of class 0 (so the reason is the 25 percent equity test alone).
--   The readings default to `base readings`: the member bank is not its own affiliate; one board at a time;
--   "directly" means the controller's own holdings and elections; prong (11) means subsidiaries of companies
--   described in prongs (1) to (10).  The purpose defaults to section 23A.
--   Section `Self-tests of the helpers` and section `Fixtures are well-formed` pass against the stubs on purpose:
--   they check this file's own list helpers and fixture spellings and are not tests of the encoding.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `regw-nouns`
IMPORT `regw-control`
IMPORT `regw-affiliate`

§ `Party builders`

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
corp MEANS Party OF n, Corporation, FALSE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
indiv MEANS Party OF n, Individual, FALSE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

GIVEN
    n IS A STRING
    k IS A `Party kind`
GIVETH A Party
`party of kind` MEANS Party OF n, k, FALSE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
depinst MEANS Party OF n, Corporation, TRUE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
finsub MEANS Party OF n, Corporation, FALSE, TRUE, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
`biz trust` MEANS Party OF n, `Business trust`, FALSE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
pship MEANS Party OF n, Partnership, FALSE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
premco MEANS Party OF n, Corporation, FALSE, FALSE, `Holds the premises of the member bank`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
safeco MEANS Party OF n, Corporation, FALSE, FALSE, `Conducts a safe deposit business`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
usco MEANS Party OF n, Corporation, FALSE, FALSE, `Holds obligations of the United States or its agencies`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
dpcin MEANS Party OF n, Corporation, FALSE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Held through a debt previously contracted, within the authorized period`, FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
dpcexp MEANS Party OF n, Corporation, FALSE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Held through a debt previously contracted, period expired`, FALSE

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
esop MEANS Party OF n, `Business trust`, FALSE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, TRUE

`the bank` MEANS Party OF "Bank", Corporation, TRUE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

§ `Holding and link builders`

-- A voting holding: percent of class is the point; equity capital is 0.
GIVEN
    h  IS A STRING
    i  IS A STRING
    c  IS A STRING
    pc IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Holding
vote MEANS Holding OF h, i, c, pc, 0, FALSE, FALSE

-- A convertible instrument: percent of class is what it would convert into.
GIVEN
    h  IS A STRING
    i  IS A STRING
    c  IS A STRING
    pc IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Holding
convertible MEANS Holding OF h, i, c, pc, 0, TRUE, FALSE

-- Shares held in a fiduciary capacity.
GIVEN
    h  IS A STRING
    i  IS A STRING
    c  IS A STRING
    pc IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Holding
fiduciary MEANS Holding OF h, i, c, pc, 0, FALSE, TRUE

-- Nonvoting equity: percent of class 0, percent of equity capital is the point.
GIVEN
    h IS A STRING
    i IS A STRING
    e IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Holding
`equity only` MEANS Holding OF h, i, "Preferred", 0, e, FALSE, FALSE

-- One row that carries both a voting percentage and an equity percentage.
GIVEN
    h  IS A STRING
    i  IS A STRING
    c  IS A STRING
    pc IS A NUMBER
    e  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Holding
`vote and equity` MEANS Holding OF h, i, c, pc, e, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN
    a IS A STRING
    b IS A STRING
GIVETH A Link
lk MEANS Link OF a, b

§ `Structure builders`

-- Every fixture has the member bank "Bank" in its parties, added here.
GIVEN
    ps  IS A LIST OF Party
    hs  IS A LIST OF Holding
    el  IS A LIST OF Link
    de  IS A LIST OF Link
    off IS A LIST OF Link
    sp  IS A LIST OF Link
    gp  IS A LIST OF Link
    da  IS A LIST OF STRING
    sh  IS A LIST OF Link
GIVETH A Structure
`full structure` MEANS Structure OF "Bank", (`the bank` FOLLOWED BY ps), hs, el, de, off, sp, gp, da, sh

GIVEN
    ps IS A LIST OF Party
    hs IS A LIST OF Holding
GIVETH A Structure
held MEANS `full structure` ps hs EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN
    ps IS A LIST OF Party
    hs IS A LIST OF Holding
    el IS A LIST OF Link
GIVETH A Structure
`with elections` MEANS `full structure` ps hs el EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN
    ps IS A LIST OF Party
    hs IS A LIST OF Holding
    de IS A LIST OF Link
GIVETH A Structure
`with determinations` MEANS `full structure` ps hs EMPTY de EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN
    ps  IS A LIST OF Party
    hs  IS A LIST OF Holding
    off IS A LIST OF Link
GIVETH A Structure
`with offices` MEANS `full structure` ps hs EMPTY EMPTY off EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN
    ps IS A LIST OF Party
    hs IS A LIST OF Holding
    sp IS A LIST OF Link
GIVETH A Structure
`with sponsorships` MEANS `full structure` ps hs EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY sp EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN
    ps IS A LIST OF Party
    hs IS A LIST OF Holding
    gp IS A LIST OF Link
GIVETH A Structure
`with general partners` MEANS `full structure` ps hs EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY gp EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN
    ps IS A LIST OF Party
    hs IS A LIST OF Holding
    da IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A Structure
`with determined affiliates` MEANS `full structure` ps hs EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY da EMPTY

GIVEN
    ps IS A LIST OF Party
    hs IS A LIST OF Holding
    sh IS A LIST OF Link
GIVETH A Structure
`with showings` MEANS `full structure` ps hs EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY sh

§ `The readings`

`base readings` MEANS Readings OF `The member bank is not its own affiliate`, `One board at a time: the member bank, or one controlling company`, `Control through the controller's own holdings and elections, without attribution`, `A subsidiary of a company described in paragraphs (a)(1) through (10) only`

`literal self readings` MEANS Readings OF `The member bank is its own affiliate on the literal words`, `One board at a time: the member bank, or one controlling company`, `Control through the controller's own holdings and elections, without attribution`, `A subsidiary of a company described in paragraphs (a)(1) through (10) only`

`pooled readings` MEANS Readings OF `The member bank is not its own affiliate`, `The offices of the member bank and of every controlling company pooled`, `Control through the controller's own holdings and elections, without attribution`, `A subsidiary of a company described in paragraphs (a)(1) through (10) only`

`any control readings` MEANS Readings OF `The member bank is not its own affiliate`, `One board at a time: the member bank, or one controlling company`, `Any control, including securities attributed from subsidiaries`, `A subsidiary of a company described in paragraphs (a)(1) through (10) only`

`chain readings` MEANS Readings OF `The member bank is not its own affiliate`, `One board at a time: the member bank, or one controlling company`, `Control through the controller's own holdings and elections, without attribution`, `A subsidiary of any affiliate, so that the prong chains`

§ `Helpers`

GIVEN
    ls IS A LIST OF Link
    a  IS A STRING
    b  IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t linked` MEANS
    CONSIDER ls
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN (x's from EQUALS a AND x's to EQUALS b) OR `t linked` xs a b

GIVEN
    l IS A LIST OF STRING
    x IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t has` MEANS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN y FOLLOWED BY ys THEN y EQUALS x OR `t has` ys x

GIVEN l IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
`t count` MEANS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN y FOLLOWED BY ys THEN 1 + `t count` ys

GIVEN
    a IS A LIST OF STRING
    b IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t all in` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN y FOLLOWED BY ys THEN `t has` b y AND `t all in` ys b

-- Two lists of names hold the same names, each once.
GIVEN
    a IS A LIST OF STRING
    b IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t same names` MEANS `t all in` a b AND `t all in` b a AND `t count` a EQUALS `t count` b

GIVEN l IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t unique` MEANS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN y FOLLOWED BY ys THEN (NOT (`t has` ys y)) AND `t unique` ys

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t agree` MEANS (a AND b) OR ((NOT (a)) AND (NOT (b)))

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF Party
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`t names of` MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN p's name FOLLOWED BY `t names of` rest

GIVEN s IS A Structure
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`t names` MEANS `t names of` (s's `the parties`)

GIVEN
    ns IS A LIST OF STRING
    hs IS A LIST OF Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t holdings named` MEANS
    CONSIDER hs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN h FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `t has` ns (h's holder) AND `t has` ns (h's issuer) AND `t holdings named` ns rest

GIVEN
    ns IS A LIST OF STRING
    ls IS A LIST OF Link
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t links named` MEANS
    CONSIDER ls
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `t has` ns (x's from) AND `t has` ns (x's to) AND `t links named` ns rest

GIVEN
    ns IS A LIST OF STRING
    ls IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t strings named` MEANS `t all in` ls ns

-- A fixture is well-formed when "Bank" is a party, names are unique, and every name used anywhere is a party.
GIVEN s IS A Structure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t wf` MEANS
    `t has` (`t names` s) (s's `the member bank`)
    AND `t unique` (`t names` s)
    AND `t holdings named` (`t names` s) (s's holdings)
    AND `t links named` (`t names` s) (s's elections)
    AND `t links named` (`t names` s) (s's determinations)
    AND `t links named` (`t names` s) (s's offices)
    AND `t links named` (`t names` s) (s's sponsorships)
    AND `t links named` (`t names` s) (s's `general partners`)
    AND `t links named` (`t names` s) (s's showings)
    AND `t strings named` (`t names` s) (s's `determined affiliates`)

-- The property every affiliate test relies on: asking about each party one at a time agrees with the list.
GIVEN
    s  IS A Structure
    r  IS A Readings
    pu IS A Purpose
    ns IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t consistent` MEANS
    CONSIDER ns
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN n FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `t agree` (`is an affiliate` s r pu n) (`t has` (`affiliates of the member bank` s r pu) n) AND `t consistent` s r pu rest

GIVEN
    s IS A Structure
    a IS A STRING
    b IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
controls MEANS `t linked` (`control relation` s) a b

GIVEN
    s IS A Structure
    a IS A STRING
    b IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`directly controls` MEANS `t linked` (`direct control relation` s) a b

-- Is the party called n an affiliate under the base readings, for section 23A?
GIVEN
    s IS A Structure
    n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`aff A` MEANS `is an affiliate` s `base readings` `Section 23A` n

-- The same for subpart F (section 23B).
GIVEN
    s IS A Structure
    n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`aff F` MEANS `is an affiliate` s `base readings` `Subpart F, section 23B` n

GIVEN
    r IS A Readings
    s IS A Structure
    n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`aff A as` MEANS `is an affiliate` s r `Section 23A` n

GIVEN
    r IS A Readings
    s IS A Structure
    n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`aff F as` MEANS `is an affiliate` s r `Subpart F, section 23B` n

GIVEN s IS A Structure
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`names A` MEANS `affiliates of the member bank` s `base readings` `Section 23A`

GIVEN s IS A Structure
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`names F` MEANS `affiliates of the member bank` s `base readings` `Subpart F, section 23B`

GIVEN
    s   IS A Structure
    cur IS A LIST OF STRING
    p   IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`step A` MEANS `affiliate step` (`inquiry about` s `base readings` `Section 23A`) cur p

GIVEN
    s   IS A Structure
    cur IS A LIST OF STRING
    p   IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`step F` MEANS `affiliate step` (`inquiry about` s `base readings` `Subpart F, section 23B`) cur p

GIVEN
    r   IS A Readings
    s   IS A Structure
    cur IS A LIST OF STRING
    p   IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`step A as` MEANS `affiliate step` (`inquiry about` s r `Section 23A`) cur p

GIVEN k IS A `Party kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`kind is a company` MEANS `is a company` (held (LIST (`party of kind` "X" k)) EMPTY) (`party of kind` "X" k)

GIVEN k IS A `Party kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`kind is a person` MEANS `is a person` (held (LIST (`party of kind` "X" k)) EMPTY) (`party of kind` "X" k)

§ `Self-tests of the helpers`

-- These pass against the stubs on purpose: they check this file's own helpers, so that a helper that
-- always answers FALSE cannot hide behind the stubs.  They are not tests of the encoding.
#ASSERT `t linked` (LIST (lk "A" "B"), (lk "C" "D")) "C" "D"
#ASSERT NOT (`t linked` (LIST (lk "A" "B")) "B" "A")
#ASSERT NOT (`t linked` EMPTY "A" "B")
#ASSERT `t has` (LIST "A", "B") "B"
#ASSERT NOT (`t has` (LIST "A", "B") "C")
#ASSERT `t count` (LIST "A", "B", "C") EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `t same names` (LIST "A", "B") (LIST "B", "A")
#ASSERT NOT (`t same names` (LIST "A", "B") (LIST "B", "C"))
#ASSERT NOT (`t same names` (LIST "A") (LIST "A", "B"))
#ASSERT `t unique` (LIST "A", "B")
#ASSERT NOT (`t unique` (LIST "A", "A"))
#ASSERT `t agree` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `t agree` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`t agree` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `t wf` (held (LIST (corp "P")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30)))
#ASSERT NOT (`t wf` (held (LIST (corp "P")) (LIST (vote "P" "Ghost" "Common" 30))))
#ASSERT NOT (`t wf` (held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "P")) EMPTY))
#ASSERT NOT (`t wf` (`with elections` (LIST (corp "P")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "P" "Ghost"))))
#ASSERT NOT (`t wf` (`with determined affiliates` (LIST (corp "P")) EMPTY (LIST "Ghost")))
#ASSERT `t same names` (`t names` (held (LIST (corp "P")) EMPTY)) (LIST "Bank", "P")

§ `223.3(f) Company`

-- "Company means a corporation, partnership, limited liability company, business trust, association,
-- or similar organization and, unless specifically excluded, includes a member bank and a depository institution."
#ASSERT `kind is a company` Corporation
#ASSERT `kind is a company` Partnership
#ASSERT `kind is a company` `Limited liability company`
#ASSERT `kind is a company` `Business trust`
#ASSERT `kind is a company` Association
#ASSERT `kind is a company` `Similar organization`
-- Not in the list: an individual, a (non-business) trust, a sole proprietorship.
#ASSERT NOT (`kind is a company` Individual)
#ASSERT NOT (`kind is a company` Trust)
#ASSERT NOT (`kind is a company` `Sole proprietorship`)
-- "includes a member bank"
#ASSERT `is a company` (held EMPTY EMPTY) `the bank`
-- "includes ... a depository institution" (a corporation that is also a depository institution)
#ASSERT `is a company` (held (LIST (depinst "D")) EMPTY) (depinst "D")

§ `223.3(bb) Person`

-- "Person means an individual, company, trust, joint venture, pool, syndicate, sole proprietorship,
-- unincorporated organization, or any other form of entity."  Every kind of party is a person.
#ASSERT `kind is a person` Individual
#ASSERT `kind is a person` Corporation
#ASSERT `kind is a person` Partnership
#ASSERT `kind is a person` `Limited liability company`
#ASSERT `kind is a person` `Business trust`
#ASSERT `kind is a person` Association
#ASSERT `kind is a person` `Similar organization`
#ASSERT `kind is a person` Trust
#ASSERT `kind is a person` `Joint venture`
#ASSERT `kind is a person` Pool
#ASSERT `kind is a person` Syndicate
#ASSERT `kind is a person` `Sole proprietorship`
#ASSERT `kind is a person` `Unincorporated organization`
#ASSERT `kind is a person` `Other form of entity`
-- the member bank is a person (it is a company)
#ASSERT `is a person` (held EMPTY EMPTY) `the bank`

§ `223.3(ii) Subsidiary`

-- "Subsidiary with respect to a specified company means a company that is controlled by the specified company."
-- The subsidiary relation is read off a list of control links (controller first).
`rel XY` MEANS LIST (lk "X" "Y")
`rel XY XZ` MEANS LIST (lk "X" "Y"), (lk "X" "Z")
`rel chain` MEANS LIST (lk "A" "B"), (lk "B" "C")
#ASSERT `is a subsidiary of` `rel XY` "X" "Y"
#ASSERT `is a subsidiary of` `rel XY XZ` "X" "Z"
#ASSERT `is a subsidiary of` `rel XY XZ` "X" "Y"
-- not symmetric: Y does not control X
#ASSERT NOT (`is a subsidiary of` `rel XY` "Y" "X")
#ASSERT NOT (`is a subsidiary of` `rel XY` "X" "Z")
#ASSERT NOT (`is a subsidiary of` `rel XY` "W" "Y")
#ASSERT NOT (`is a subsidiary of` EMPTY "X" "Y")
-- B is controlled by A, and C by B: each of those links is read off the list
#ASSERT `is a subsidiary of` `rel chain` "B" "C"
#ASSERT `is a subsidiary of` `rel chain` "A" "B"

§ `223.3(g)(1)(i) Control by 25 percent of a class of voting securities`

-- "owns, controls, or has power to vote 25 percent or more of any class of voting securities of the other company"
`f c25` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "Common" 25))
`f c24` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "Common" 24.9))
`f c30` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "Common" 30))
-- "25 percent or more": exactly 25 is enough, just under is not
#ASSERT controls `f c25` "P" "T"
#ASSERT controls `f c30` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f c24` "P" "T")
-- control is of a company by a controller, not the reverse
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f c30` "T" "P")

-- "any class": more than one class, each held at a different percentage
`f two classes below` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "A" 20), (vote "P" "T" "B" 20))
`f one class above` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "A" 10), (vote "P" "T" "B" 30))
-- 20 percent of A and 20 percent of B is not 25 percent of any one class, however the two add up
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f two classes below` "P" "T")
-- 30 percent of class B is enough though only 10 percent of class A is held
#ASSERT controls `f one class above` "P" "T"

-- more than one holder of one class: each holder is looked at on its own
`f two holders below` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P1"), (corp "P2"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P1" "T" "Common" 20), (vote "P2" "T" "Common" 20))
`f two holders above` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P1"), (corp "P2"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P1" "T" "Common" 30), (vote "P2" "T" "Common" 30))
`f two holders one above` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P1"), (corp "P2"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P1" "T" "Common" 30), (vote "P2" "T" "Common" 20))
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f two holders below` "P1" "T")
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f two holders below` "P2" "T")
#ASSERT controls `f two holders above` "P1" "T"
#ASSERT controls `f two holders above` "P2" "T"
#ASSERT controls `f two holders one above` "P1" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f two holders one above` "P2" "T")

-- "the company or shareholder": an individual shareholder controls as a company does
`f individual holder` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "I" "T" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f individual holder` "I" "T"

-- "of the other company": the controlled party is a company; a (non-business) trust is not
`f issuer is a trust` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (`party of kind` "T" Trust)) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "Common" 30))
`f issuer is an llc` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (`party of kind` "T" `Limited liability company`)) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f issuer is a trust` "P" "T")
#ASSERT controls `f issuer is an llc` "P" "T"

-- the member bank as controller and as controlled
`f bank is the controller` MEANS held (LIST (corp "S")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "S" "Common" 30))
`f bank is controlled` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 25))
#ASSERT controls `f bank is the controller` "Bank" "S"
#ASSERT controls `f bank is controlled` "P" "Bank"

§ `223.3(g)(1)(ii) and (iii) Control by election and by determination`

-- (ii): "controls in any manner the election of a majority of the directors, trustees, or general partners"
`f elected` MEANS `with elections` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T"), (corp "Q")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "P" "T"))
#ASSERT controls `f elected` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f elected` "T" "P")
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f elected` "Q" "T")
-- direct control counts the controller's own elections
#ASSERT `directly controls` `f elected` "P" "T"

-- (iii): "The Board determines, after notice and opportunity for hearing, that the company or shareholder ...
-- exercises a controlling influence over the management or policies of the other company"
`f determined` MEANS `with determinations` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T"), (corp "Q")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "P" "T"))
#ASSERT controls `f determined` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f determined` "T" "P")
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f determined` "Q" "T")
#ASSERT `directly controls` `f determined` "P" "T"

§ `223.3(g)(2) Shares held as fiduciary`

-- "no company will be deemed to control another company by virtue of its ownership or control of shares in a
-- fiduciary capacity, except as provided in paragraph (a)(3) of § 223.2 or if the company owning or controlling
-- the shares is a business trust."
`f fiduciary 30` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (fiduciary "P" "T" "Common" 30))
`f fiduciary business trust` MEANS held (LIST (`biz trust` "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (fiduciary "P" "T" "Common" 30))
`f fiduciary plus own` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "Common" 25), (fiduciary "P" "T" "Common" 10))
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f fiduciary 30` "P" "T")
-- "or if the company owning or controlling the shares is a business trust"
#ASSERT controls `f fiduciary business trust` "P" "T"
-- 25 percent held on its own account is control whatever else is held as fiduciary
#ASSERT controls `f fiduciary plus own` "P" "T"

-- a trustee that has nothing to do with the member bank, and shares of the member bank itself held as fiduciary
`f fiduciary stranger` MEANS held (LIST (corp "TC"), (corp "Co")) (LIST (fiduciary "TC" "Co" "Common" 30))
`f fiduciary of the bank` MEANS held (LIST (corp "TC")) (LIST (fiduciary "TC" "Bank" "Common" 30))
`f fiduciary of the bank business trust` MEANS held (LIST (`biz trust` "TC")) (LIST (fiduciary "TC" "Bank" "Common" 30))
-- a trustee unconnected with the member bank: nothing makes its company an affiliate
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f fiduciary stranger` "Co")
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f fiduciary stranger` "TC")
-- shares of the member bank held only as fiduciary do not make the holder its parent, unless it is a business trust
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f fiduciary of the bank` "TC")
#ASSERT `aff A` `f fiduciary of the bank business trust` "TC"

§ `223.3(g)(3) Securities owned or controlled by a subsidiary`

-- "A company controls securities, assets, or other ownership interests owned or controlled, directly or indirectly,
-- by any subsidiary (including a subsidiary depository institution) of the company."
-- One level: P controls S (30 percent) and S holds 30 percent of T, so P controls T (the percentages do not multiply).
`f one level` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S" "Common" 30), (vote "S" "T" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f one level` "P" "S"
#ASSERT controls `f one level` "S" "T"
#ASSERT controls `f one level` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f one level` "T" "P")
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f one level` "S" "P")
-- direct control is the controller's own holdings only
#ASSERT `directly controls` `f one level` "P" "S"
#ASSERT `directly controls` `f one level` "S" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (`directly controls` `f one level` "P" "T")

-- exactly 25 percent at the second level is enough to be attributed whole
`f one level 25` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S" "Common" 30), (vote "S" "T" "Common" 25))
#ASSERT controls `f one level 25` "P" "T"

-- Two levels: P controls S1, S1 controls S2, S2 holds 30 percent of T.
`f two levels` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S1"), (corp "S2"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S1" "Common" 30), (vote "S1" "S2" "Common" 30), (vote "S2" "T" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f two levels` "P" "S2"
#ASSERT controls `f two levels` "S1" "T"
#ASSERT controls `f two levels` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (`directly controls` `f two levels` "P" "T")
#ASSERT NOT (`directly controls` `f two levels` "S1" "T")
#ASSERT `directly controls` `f two levels` "S2" "T"

-- "any subsidiary": a company that does not control S does not get S's holdings
`f not a subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S" "Common" 20), (vote "S" "T" "Common" 60))
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f not a subsidiary` "P" "S")
#ASSERT controls `f not a subsidiary` "S" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f not a subsidiary` "P" "T")

-- what the controller owns itself and what its subsidiary owns are added within one class
`f added` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "T" "Common" 15), (vote "S" "T" "Common" 10))
`f added classes` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "T" "A" 15), (vote "S" "T" "B" 10))
`f added three` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "T" "Common" 5), (vote "S" "T" "Common" 20))
#ASSERT controls `f added` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f added` "S" "T")
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f added classes` "P" "T")
#ASSERT controls `f added three` "P" "T"

-- a subsidiary's shares held as fiduciary are not attributed ((g)(2))
`f subsidiary fiduciary` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S" "Common" 30), (fiduciary "S" "T" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f subsidiary fiduciary` "P" "T")
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f subsidiary fiduciary` "S" "T")

-- "other ownership interests": equity capital is attributed too, and added to the controller's own
`f equity added` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S" "Common" 30), (`equity only` "P" "T" 15), (`equity only` "S" "T" 10))
#ASSERT controls `f equity added` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f equity added` "S" "T")

-- a subsidiary is a company controlled by the specified company, in any of the ways of (g)(1): here by election
`f subsidiary by election` MEANS `with elections` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "S" "T" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "P" "S"))
#ASSERT controls `f subsidiary by election` "P" "S"
#ASSERT controls `f subsidiary by election` "P" "T"

-- "(including a subsidiary depository institution)"
`f subsidiary di` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (depinst "D"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "D" "Common" 30), (vote "D" "T" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f subsidiary di` "P" "T"

-- siblings do not share: S2 is not S1's controller
`f siblings` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S1"), (corp "S2"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S1" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "S2" "Common" 30), (vote "S1" "T" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f siblings` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f siblings` "S2" "T")
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f siblings` "S2" "S1")

§ `223.3(g) control step: what a company controls through its subsidiaries, given a list of control links`

-- The list `rel` is taken as already established.  The structures never carry a holding between the
-- controller and its subsidiary, so the answer cannot depend on whether the step derives or reads the link.
`f step own and sub` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "Common" 15), (vote "S" "T" "Common" 10))
`f step sub` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "S" "T" "Common" 30))
`f step two levels` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S1"), (corp "S2"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "S2" "T" "Common" 30))
`f step elected` MEANS `with elections` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "P" "T"))
`f step determined` MEANS `with determinations` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "P" "T"))
`f step fiduciary` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (fiduciary "S" "T" "Common" 30))
`f step convertible` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (convertible "S" "T" "Common" 30))
`f step equity` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (`equity only` "S" "T" 25))
-- "controls securities ... owned or controlled by any subsidiary": 15 own plus 10 through S is 25
#ASSERT `control step` `f step own and sub` (LIST (lk "P" "S")) "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (`control step` `f step own and sub` EMPTY "P" "T")
-- S is not shown to be P's subsidiary the other way round
#ASSERT NOT (`control step` `f step own and sub` (LIST (lk "S" "P")) "P" "T")
#ASSERT NOT (`control step` `f step own and sub` EMPTY "S" "T")
#ASSERT `control step` `f step sub` (LIST (lk "P" "S")) "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (`control step` `f step sub` EMPTY "P" "T")
#ASSERT `control step` `f step sub` EMPTY "S" "T"
-- "owned or controlled, directly or indirectly, by any subsidiary": S2's shares reach P, whose list holds both subsidiaries
-- (the list is closed: it holds (P, S2) as well as the two links through S1; see R15 for the list that is not)
#ASSERT `control step` `f step two levels` (LIST (lk "P" "S1"), (lk "S1" "S2"), (lk "P" "S2")) "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (`control step` `f step two levels` (LIST (lk "P" "S1")) "P" "T")
-- election and determination are the controller's own, whatever the list holds
#ASSERT `control step` `f step elected` EMPTY "P" "T"
#ASSERT `control step` `f step determined` EMPTY "P" "T"
-- the same exclusions and inclusions as for control itself, seen through a subsidiary
#ASSERT NOT (`control step` `f step fiduciary` (LIST (lk "P" "S")) "P" "T")
#ASSERT `control step` `f step convertible` (LIST (lk "P" "S")) "P" "T"
#ASSERT `control step` `f step equity` (LIST (lk "P" "S")) "P" "T"

§ `223.3(g)(4) Convertible instruments`

-- "A company or shareholder that owns or controls instruments (including options or warrants) that are convertible or
-- exercisable, at the option of the holder or owner, into securities, controls the securities, unless the company or
-- shareholder presents information to the Board that demonstrates, to the Board's satisfaction, that the company or
-- shareholder should not be deemed to control the securities."
`f convertible 30` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (convertible "P" "T" "Common" 30))
`f convertible 20` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (convertible "P" "T" "Common" 20))
`f convertible added` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (convertible "P" "T" "Common" 15), (vote "P" "T" "Common" 10))
`f convertible other class` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (convertible "P" "T" "A" 15), (vote "P" "T" "B" 10))
`f convertible shown` MEANS `with showings` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (convertible "P" "T" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "P" "T"))
`f convertible shown plus own` MEANS `with showings` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (convertible "P" "T" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "T" "Common" 25)) (LIST (lk "P" "T"))
`f convertible shown added` MEANS `with showings` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (convertible "P" "T" "Common" 15), (vote "P" "T" "Common" 10)) (LIST (lk "P" "T"))
`f convertible shown elsewhere` MEANS `with showings` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "Q"), (corp "T")) (LIST (convertible "P" "T" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "P" "Q"))
`f convertible shown by another` MEANS `with showings` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "Q"), (corp "T")) (LIST (convertible "P" "T" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "Q" "T"))
`f convertible by subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S" "Common" 30), (convertible "S" "T" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f convertible 30` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f convertible 20` "P" "T")
-- the securities it could acquire are added to those it owns, within one class
#ASSERT controls `f convertible added` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f convertible other class` "P" "T")
-- the showing removes the convertible securities only
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f convertible shown` "P" "T")
#ASSERT controls `f convertible shown plus own` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f convertible shown added` "P" "T")
-- a showing about another issuer, or by another holder, does not help
#ASSERT controls `f convertible shown elsewhere` "P" "T"
#ASSERT controls `f convertible shown by another` "P" "T"
-- the subsidiary controls the securities it could acquire, and the parent controls what the subsidiary controls
#ASSERT controls `f convertible by subsidiary` "S" "T"
#ASSERT controls `f convertible by subsidiary` "P" "T"

§ `223.3(g)(5) Nonvoting securities`

-- "A company or shareholder that owns or controls 25 percent or more of the equity capital of another company controls the
-- other company, unless the company or shareholder presents information to the Board that demonstrates, to the Board's
-- satisfaction, that the company or shareholder does not control the other company."
`f equity 25` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (`equity only` "P" "T" 25))
`f equity 24` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (`equity only` "P" "T" 24))
`f equity individual` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "T")) (LIST (`equity only` "I" "T" 25))
`f equity shown` MEANS `with showings` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (`equity only` "P" "T" 30)) (LIST (lk "P" "T"))
`f equity shown by another` MEANS `with showings` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "Q"), (corp "T")) (LIST (`equity only` "P" "T" 30)) (LIST (lk "Q" "T"))
`f equity vote below` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (`vote and equity` "P" "T" "Common" 10 20))
`f equity vote below equity at` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (`vote and equity` "P" "T" "Common" 10 25))
`f equity by subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S" "Common" 30), (`equity only` "S" "T" 25))
#ASSERT controls `f equity 25` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f equity 24` "P" "T")
#ASSERT controls `f equity individual` "I" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f equity shown` "P" "T")
#ASSERT controls `f equity shown by another` "P" "T"
-- neither test is met: 10 percent of a voting class, 20 percent of the equity capital
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f equity vote below` "P" "T")
-- the equity test is met by the same row though the voting test is not
#ASSERT controls `f equity vote below equity at` "P" "T"
#ASSERT controls `f equity by subsidiary` "P" "T"

§ `223.2(a)(1) Parent companies`

-- "Any company that controls the member bank"
`f p30` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30))
`f p24` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 24))
`f p individual` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I")) (LIST (vote "I" "Bank" "Common" 30))
`f p elected` MEANS `with elections` (LIST (corp "P")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "P" "Bank"))
`f p determined` MEANS `with determinations` (LIST (corp "P")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "P" "Bank"))
`f p equity` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P")) (LIST (`equity only` "P" "Bank" 25))
`f p convertible` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P")) (LIST (convertible "P" "Bank" "Common" 30))
`f p indirect` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "M")) (LIST (vote "P" "M" "Common" 30), (vote "M" "Bank" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f p30` "P"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f p24` "P")
-- "Any company": an individual who controls the member bank is not a company, so not an affiliate under this prong
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f p individual` "I")
-- control in any of the ways of 223.3(g)
#ASSERT `aff A` `f p elected` "P"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f p determined` "P"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f p equity` "P"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f p convertible` "P"
-- through a subsidiary: P controls M, M holds 30 percent of the member bank
#ASSERT `aff A` `f p indirect` "M"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f p indirect` "P"
-- the exclusion for fiduciary shares ((g)(2)) is in `223.3(g)(2)`; the parent test for a plain 25 is here
`f p exactly 25` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 25))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f p exactly 25` "P"
-- and the same prong through the step function, which needs no earlier affiliate
#ASSERT `step A` `f p30` EMPTY (corp "P")
#ASSERT NOT (`step A` `f p24` EMPTY (corp "P"))

§ `223.2(a)(2) Companies under common control by a parent company`

-- "Any company, including any subsidiary of the member bank, that is controlled by a company that controls the member bank"
`f sibling` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "C" "Common" 30))
`f sibling below` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "C" "Common" 24))
`f sibling elected` MEANS `with elections` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "P" "C"))
`f sibling through subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "S" "Common" 30), (vote "S" "C" "Common" 30))
`f sibling and bank subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "Sub")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 60), (vote "P" "Sub" "Common" 30))
`f sibling of a non-parent` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "I" "Bank" "Common" 10), (vote "I" "C" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f sibling` "C"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f sibling below` "C")
#ASSERT `aff A` `f sibling elected` "C"
-- C is controlled through a subsidiary of P: P controls S, and S holds 30 percent of C
#ASSERT `aff A` `f sibling through subsidiary` "S"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f sibling through subsidiary` "C"
-- "including any subsidiary of the member bank": a subsidiary of the member bank that the parent itself holds 30 percent of
-- (it is directly controlled by an affiliate, so 223.2(b)(1)(iii)(A) lets it back in)
#ASSERT `aff A` `f sibling and bank subsidiary` "Sub"
-- a company controlled by a person who does not control the member bank is not in this prong
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f sibling of a non-parent` "C")
#ASSERT `step A` `f sibling` EMPTY (corp "C")

§ `223.2(a)(3) Companies under other common control`

-- "Any company, including any subsidiary of the member bank, that is controlled, directly or indirectly, by trust or otherwise,
-- by or for the benefit of shareholders who beneficially or otherwise control, directly or indirectly, by trust or otherwise,
-- the member bank or any company that controls the member bank"
`f shareholder` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "I" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "I" "C" "Common" 30))
`f shareholder below` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "I" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "I" "C" "Common" 24))
`f shareholder weak` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "I" "Bank" "Common" 10), (vote "I" "C" "Common" 30))
`f shareholder of a parent` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "P"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "I" "P" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "I" "C" "Common" 30))
`f shareholder through a company` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "Mid"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "I" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "I" "Mid" "Common" 30), (vote "Mid" "C" "Common" 30))
`f shareholder equity` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "I" "Bank" "Common" 30), (`equity only` "I" "C" 25))
`f shareholder elected` MEANS `with elections` (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "I" "Bank" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "I" "C"))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f shareholder` "C"
-- the individual is a shareholder, not a company
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f shareholder` "I")
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f shareholder below` "C")
-- the shareholder must itself control the member bank (10 percent does not)
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f shareholder weak` "C")
-- "or any company that controls the member bank": the shareholder controls P, which controls the member bank
#ASSERT `aff A` `f shareholder of a parent` "C"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f shareholder of a parent` "P"
-- "directly or indirectly": Mid is controlled by I, and Mid holds 30 percent of C
#ASSERT `aff A` `f shareholder through a company` "Mid"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f shareholder through a company` "C"
-- control in the other ways of (g)
#ASSERT `aff A` `f shareholder equity` "C"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f shareholder elected` "C"
#ASSERT `step A` `f shareholder` EMPTY (corp "C")

§ `223.2(a)(4) Companies with interlocking directorates`

-- "Any company in which a majority of its directors, trustees, or general partners (or individuals exercising similar functions)
-- constitute a majority of the persons holding any such office with the member bank or any company that controls the member bank"
-- Offices are links from a person to the company whose office the person holds.
-- The member bank's board is d1, d2, d3 unless the fixture says otherwise.
`f il two of three` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (corp "Co"), (indiv "d1"), (indiv "d2"), (indiv "d3"), (indiv "x1")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "d1" "Bank"), (lk "d2" "Bank"), (lk "d3" "Bank"), (lk "d1" "Co"), (lk "d2" "Co"), (lk "x1" "Co"))
`f il one of three` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (corp "Co"), (indiv "d1"), (indiv "d2"), (indiv "d3"), (indiv "x1"), (indiv "x2")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "d1" "Bank"), (lk "d2" "Bank"), (lk "d3" "Bank"), (lk "d1" "Co"), (lk "x1" "Co"), (lk "x2" "Co"))
`f il all of three on a larger board` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (corp "Co"), (indiv "d1"), (indiv "d2"), (indiv "d3"), (indiv "w1"), (indiv "w2")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "d1" "Bank"), (lk "d2" "Bank"), (lk "d3" "Bank"), (lk "d1" "Co"), (lk "d2" "Co"), (lk "d3" "Co"), (lk "w1" "Co"), (lk "w2" "Co"))
`f il exactly half` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (corp "Co"), (indiv "d1"), (indiv "d2"), (indiv "d3"), (indiv "d4"), (indiv "e1"), (indiv "e2")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "d1" "Bank"), (lk "d2" "Bank"), (lk "d3" "Bank"), (lk "d4" "Bank"), (lk "d1" "Co"), (lk "d2" "Co"), (lk "e1" "Co"), (lk "e2" "Co"))
`f il sole director` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (corp "Co"), (indiv "d1"), (indiv "d2"), (indiv "d3")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "d1" "Bank"), (lk "d2" "Bank"), (lk "d3" "Bank"), (lk "d1" "Co"))
`f il sole bank director` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (corp "Co"), (indiv "d1"), (indiv "e1"), (indiv "e2")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "d1" "Bank"), (lk "d1" "Co"), (lk "e1" "Co"), (lk "e2" "Co"))
`f il same board` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (corp "Co"), (indiv "d1"), (indiv "d2")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "d1" "Bank"), (lk "d2" "Bank"), (lk "d1" "Co"), (lk "d2" "Co"))
`f il parent board` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "Co"), (indiv "b1"), (indiv "b2"), (indiv "b3"), (indiv "p1"), (indiv "p2"), (indiv "p3"), (indiv "x1")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "b1" "Bank"), (lk "b2" "Bank"), (lk "b3" "Bank"), (lk "p1" "P"), (lk "p2" "P"), (lk "p3" "P"), (lk "p1" "Co"), (lk "p2" "Co"), (lk "x1" "Co"))
`f il parent board entire` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "Co"), (indiv "b1"), (indiv "p1"), (indiv "p2"), (indiv "p3")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "b1" "Bank"), (lk "p1" "P"), (lk "p2" "P"), (lk "p3" "P"), (lk "p1" "Co"), (lk "p2" "Co"), (lk "p3" "Co"))
`f il stranger board` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (corp "N"), (corp "Co"), (indiv "b1"), (indiv "b2"), (indiv "b3"), (indiv "n1"), (indiv "n2"), (indiv "n3"), (indiv "x1")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "b1" "Bank"), (lk "b2" "Bank"), (lk "b3" "Bank"), (lk "n1" "N"), (lk "n2" "N"), (lk "n3" "N"), (lk "n1" "Co"), (lk "n2" "Co"), (lk "x1" "Co"))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f il two of three` "Co"
-- one director in common with a board of three is not a majority of either
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f il one of three` "Co")
-- all three of the member bank's directors sit on a board of five: three of five is a majority of the company's board
#ASSERT `aff A` `f il all of three on a larger board` "Co"
-- exactly half of each board is not a majority
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f il exactly half` "Co")
-- the company's whole board (one person) is in common, but one of three is not a majority of the member bank's persons
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f il sole director` "Co")
-- the member bank's whole board (one person) is in common, but one of three is not a majority of the company's directors
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f il sole bank director` "Co")
#ASSERT `aff A` `f il same board` "Co"
-- "or any company that controls the member bank": Co's whole board is the controlling company's whole board
-- (the member bank's board is one person; whether the boards are taken one at a time or pooled, Co is an affiliate)
#ASSERT `aff A` `f il parent board entire` "Co"
-- a company that does not control the member bank does not count
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f il stranger board` "Co")
#ASSERT `step A` `f il two of three` EMPTY (corp "Co")

§ `223.2(a)(5) Sponsored and advised companies`

-- "Any company, including a real estate investment trust, that is sponsored and advised on a contractual basis by the member bank
-- or an affiliate of the member bank"
`f sponsored reit` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (`biz trust` "Reit")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "Bank" "Reit"))
`f sponsored company` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "C")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "Bank" "C"))
`f sponsored by a stranger` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "N"), (corp "C")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "N" "C"))
`f sponsored by a parent` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "P" "C"))
`f sponsored chain` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "C1"), (corp "C2"), (corp "C3")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "Bank" "C1"), (lk "C1" "C2"))
`f sponsored trust` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (`party of kind` "T" Trust)) EMPTY (LIST (lk "Bank" "T"))
`f sponsored individual` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (indiv "I")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "Bank" "I"))
`f sponsored cycle` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "A"), (corp "B")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "A" "B"), (lk "B" "A"))
`f sponsored the other way` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "C")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "C" "Bank"))
`f sponsored by an excluded company` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "P"), (premco "Prem"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "Prem" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "Prem" "C"))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f sponsored reit` "Reit"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f sponsored company` "C"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f sponsored by a stranger` "C")
-- "or an affiliate of the member bank": sponsored by a parent
#ASSERT `aff A` `f sponsored by a parent` "C"
-- sponsored by the member bank's sponsored company: a chain through an affiliate
#ASSERT `aff A` `f sponsored chain` "C1"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f sponsored chain` "C2"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f sponsored chain` "C3")
-- "Any company": a trust that is not a business trust, and an individual, are not companies
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f sponsored trust` "T")
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f sponsored individual` "I")
-- two unconnected companies sponsoring each other do not make each other affiliates: there is no affiliate to start from
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f sponsored cycle` "A")
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f sponsored cycle` "B")
-- the member bank sponsored by C: "sponsored ... by the member bank" is the other direction
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f sponsored the other way` "C")
-- sponsored by a company that 223.2(b)(2) excludes (it is not an affiliate), so not "an affiliate of the member bank"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f sponsored by an excluded company` "Prem")
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f sponsored by an excluded company` "C")

§ `223.2(a)(7) Depository institution subsidiaries`

-- "A depository institution that is a subsidiary of the member bank"
`f di subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (depinst "Dsub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Dsub" "Common" 60))
`f non-di subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (corp "Nsub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Nsub" "Common" 60))
`f di not a subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (depinst "D")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "D" "Common" 20))
`f di through subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (corp "Mid"), (depinst "Dsub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Mid" "Common" 60), (vote "Mid" "Dsub" "Common" 60))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f di subsidiary` "Dsub"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f non-di subsidiary` "Nsub")
-- 20 percent is not control, so D is no subsidiary
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f di not a subsidiary` "D")
-- a subsidiary of a subsidiary is a subsidiary of the member bank (223.3(g)(3)); the plain middle company is not an affiliate
#ASSERT `aff A` `f di through subsidiary` "Dsub"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f di through subsidiary` "Mid")
#ASSERT `step A` `f di subsidiary` EMPTY (depinst "Dsub")

§ `223.2(a)(8) Financial subsidiaries`

-- "A financial subsidiary of the member bank"
`f financial subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (finsub "Fsub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Fsub" "Common" 60))
`f plain subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (corp "Psub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Psub" "Common" 60))
`f subsidiary of a financial subsidiary` MEANS held (LIST (finsub "Fs"), (corp "Gs")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Fs" "Common" 60), (vote "Fs" "Gs" "Common" 60))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f financial subsidiary` "Fsub"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f plain subsidiary` "Psub")
-- a subsidiary of a financial subsidiary: a subsidiary of a company described in (a)(8), directly controlled by an affiliate
#ASSERT `aff A` `f subsidiary of a financial subsidiary` "Fs"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f subsidiary of a financial subsidiary` "Gs"
#ASSERT `step A` `f financial subsidiary` EMPTY (finsub "Fsub")

§ `223.2(a)(10) Partnerships associated with the member bank or an affiliate`

-- "Any partnership for which the member bank or any affiliate of the member bank serves as a general partner or for which the
-- member bank or any affiliate of the member bank causes any director, officer, or employee ... to serve as a general partner"
`f partnership of the bank` MEANS `with general partners` (LIST (pship "Pn")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "Bank" "Pn"))
`f partnership of a stranger` MEANS `with general partners` (LIST (corp "N"), (pship "Pn")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "N" "Pn"))
`f partnership of a parent` MEANS `with general partners` (LIST (corp "P"), (pship "Pn")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "P" "Pn"))
`f general partner of a corporation` MEANS `with general partners` (LIST (corp "Co")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "Bank" "Co"))
`f partnership held by the bank` MEANS `with general partners` (LIST (pship "Pn")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Pn" "Common" 60)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "Pn"))
`f partnership as general partner of the bank` MEANS `with general partners` (LIST (pship "Pn")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "Pn" "Bank"))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f partnership of the bank` "Pn"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f partnership of a stranger` "Pn")
#ASSERT `aff A` `f partnership of a parent` "Pn"
-- "Any partnership": a corporation is not one
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f general partner of a corporation` "Co")
-- the other direction: the partnership serves as general partner of the member bank
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f partnership as general partner of the bank` "Pn")
-- a partnership that is a subsidiary of the member bank is excluded by 223.2(b)(1), though the bank is its general partner
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f partnership held by the bank` "Pn")
#ASSERT `step A` `f partnership of the bank` EMPTY (pship "Pn")
#ASSERT NOT (`step A` `f partnership of a stranger` EMPTY (pship "Pn"))

§ `223.2(a)(11) Subsidiaries of affiliates`

-- "Any subsidiary of a company described in paragraphs (a)(1) through (10) of this section"
-- C1 is sponsored by the member bank, so it is described in (a)(5); D1 is held by C1.
`f subsidiary of a sponsored company` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "C1"), (corp "D1")) (LIST (vote "C1" "D1" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "C1"))
`f subsidiary of a subsidiary` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "C1"), (corp "D1"), (corp "E1")) (LIST (vote "C1" "D1" "Common" 30), (vote "D1" "E1" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "C1"))
`f subsidiary of a stranger` MEANS held (LIST (corp "N"), (corp "D")) (LIST (vote "N" "D" "Common" 30))
`f subsidiary of a sponsored company below` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "C1"), (corp "D1")) (LIST (vote "C1" "D1" "Common" 24)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "C1"))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f subsidiary of a sponsored company` "C1"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f subsidiary of a sponsored company` "D1"
-- E1 is held by D1, which C1 controls, so C1 controls E1's securities (223.3(g)(3)) and E1 is C1's subsidiary
#ASSERT `aff A` `f subsidiary of a subsidiary` "E1"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f subsidiary of a stranger` "D")
-- 24 percent is not control, so D1 is not C1's subsidiary
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f subsidiary of a sponsored company below` "D1")

§ `223.2(a)(12) Other companies`

-- "Any company that the Board determines by regulation or order, or that the appropriate Federal banking agency ... determines by order"
`f determined company` MEANS `with determined affiliates` (LIST (corp "Det")) EMPTY (LIST "Det")
`f undetermined company` MEANS `with determined affiliates` (LIST (corp "Det")) EMPTY EMPTY
`f determined individual` MEANS `with determined affiliates` (LIST (indiv "I")) EMPTY (LIST "I")
`f determined subsidiary` MEANS `with determined affiliates` (LIST (corp "DS")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "DS" "Common" 60)) (LIST "DS")
`f undetermined subsidiary` MEANS `with determined affiliates` (LIST (corp "DS")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "DS" "Common" 60)) EMPTY
`f subsidiary of a determined company` MEANS `with determined affiliates` (LIST (corp "Det"), (corp "DS")) (LIST (vote "Det" "DS" "Common" 30)) (LIST "Det")
`f sponsored by a determined company` MEANS `full structure` (LIST (corp "Det"), (corp "C")) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (LIST (lk "Det" "C")) EMPTY (LIST "Det") EMPTY
#ASSERT `aff A` `f determined company` "Det"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f undetermined company` "Det")
-- 223.2(b)(1)(v): a subsidiary determined to be an affiliate under (a)(12) is not excluded
#ASSERT `aff A` `f determined subsidiary` "DS"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f undetermined subsidiary` "DS")
-- the prongs that speak of "an affiliate" include the ones determined under (a)(12): sponsored and advised by one
#ASSERT `aff A` `f sponsored by a determined company` "C"
-- the determination applies to the section 23B purpose too (the company is not a depository institution)
#ASSERT `aff F` `f determined company` "Det"
#ASSERT `step A` `f determined company` EMPTY (corp "Det")

§ `223.2(b)(1) Subsidiaries of the member bank`

-- "Any company that is a subsidiary of the member bank" is not an affiliate "unless the company is: (i) A depository institution;
-- (ii) A financial subsidiary; (iii) Directly controlled by: (A) One or more affiliates (other than depository institution affiliates)
-- of the member bank; or (B) A shareholder that controls the member bank ...; (iv) An employee stock option plan, trust, or similar
-- organization ...; or (v) Any other company determined to be an affiliate under paragraph (a)(12)"
-- The member bank sponsors and advises a company it holds 60 percent of: described in (a)(5), but a subsidiary, so excluded.
`f excluded subsidiary` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "Sub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 60)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "Sub"))
`f not a subsidiary sponsored` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "Sub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 20)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "Sub"))
`f subsidiary of a subsidiary excluded` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "S1"), (corp "S2")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "S1" "Common" 60), (vote "S1" "S2" "Common" 60)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "S2"))
`f subsidiary di sponsored` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (depinst "Sub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 60)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "Sub"))
`f subsidiary fs sponsored` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (finsub "Sub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 60)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "Sub"))
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f excluded subsidiary` "Sub")
-- not a subsidiary (20 percent), so nothing excludes it
#ASSERT `aff A` `f not a subsidiary sponsored` "Sub"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f subsidiary of a subsidiary excluded` "S2")
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f subsidiary of a subsidiary excluded` "S1")
-- (i) and (ii)
#ASSERT `aff A` `f subsidiary di sponsored` "Sub"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f subsidiary fs sponsored` "Sub"

-- (iii)(A): directly controlled by an affiliate that is not a depository institution
`f directly by an affiliate` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "A1"), (corp "Sub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 60), (vote "A1" "Sub" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "A1"))
`f directly by a di affiliate` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (depinst "D1"), (corp "Sub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 60), (vote "D1" "Sub" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "D1"))
`f directly by an affiliate below` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "A1"), (corp "Sub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 60), (vote "A1" "Sub" "Common" 24)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "A1"))
`f directly by election` MEANS `full structure` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "Sub")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 60)) (LIST (lk "P" "Sub")) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY
`f directly by determination` MEANS `full structure` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "Sub")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 60)) EMPTY (LIST (lk "P" "Sub")) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY
#ASSERT `aff A` `f directly by an affiliate` "A1"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f directly by an affiliate` "Sub"
-- a depository institution affiliate does not count: "(other than depository institution affiliates)"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f directly by a di affiliate` "D1"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f directly by a di affiliate` "Sub")
-- 24 percent is not control, so not directly controlled
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f directly by an affiliate below` "Sub")
-- control by the parent's own election of the subsidiary's directors, or by the Board's determination, is direct control
#ASSERT `aff A` `f directly by election` "Sub"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f directly by determination` "Sub"
-- (iii)(A) is about affiliates already found: through the step function
-- P is also "a shareholder that controls the member bank", so (iii)(B) lets Sub back in whatever is already known
#ASSERT `step A` `f sibling and bank subsidiary` EMPTY (corp "Sub")
#ASSERT NOT (`step A as` `chain readings` `f directly by an affiliate` EMPTY (corp "Sub"))
#ASSERT `step A as` `chain readings` `f directly by an affiliate` (LIST "A1") (corp "Sub")
-- a depository institution affiliate found earlier does not let the subsidiary back in
#ASSERT NOT (`step A as` `chain readings` `f directly by a di affiliate` (LIST "D1") (corp "Sub"))

-- (iii)(B): "A shareholder that controls the member bank"
`f directly by a shareholder` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "Sub")) (LIST (vote "I" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 60), (vote "I" "Sub" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f directly by a shareholder` "Sub"

-- (iv): "An employee stock option plan, trust, or similar organization that exists for the benefit of the shareholders, partners,
-- members, or employees of the member bank or any of its affiliates"
`f esop subsidiary` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (esop "Plan")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Plan" "Common" 60)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "Plan"))
`f business trust subsidiary` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (`biz trust` "Plan")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Plan" "Common" 60)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "Plan"))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f esop subsidiary` "Plan"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f business trust subsidiary` "Plan")

§ `223.2(b)(2), (3) and (4) Companies engaged solely in one activity`

-- "(2) Bank premises. Any company engaged solely in holding the premises of the member bank.
-- (3) Safe deposit. Any company engaged solely in conducting a safe deposit business.
-- (4) Government securities. Any company engaged solely in holding obligations of the United States or its agencies ..."
`f premises sibling` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (premco "Prem")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "Prem" "Common" 30))
`f safe deposit sibling` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (safeco "Safe")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "Safe" "Common" 30))
`f securities sibling` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (usco "Gov")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "Gov" "Common" 30))
`f premises parent` MEANS held (LIST (premco "P")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30))
`f premises sponsored` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (premco "Prem")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "Bank" "Prem"))
`f premises below a sibling` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (premco "PremS"), (corp "Sub2")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "PremS" "Common" 30), (vote "PremS" "Sub2" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f premises sibling` "Prem")
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f safe deposit sibling` "Safe")
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f securities sibling` "Gov")
-- the company with some other activity, same structure, is an affiliate ((a)(2) above): the activity is what changes the answer
-- the exclusion applies to a parent too, and to a sponsored company
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f premises parent` "P")
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f premises sponsored` "Prem")
-- the exclusion is of the company engaged solely in the activity, not of the companies it controls
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f premises below a sibling` "PremS")
#ASSERT `aff A` `f premises below a sibling` "Sub2"

§ `223.2(b)(5) Companies held DPC`

-- "Any company where control results from the exercise of rights arising out of a bona fide debt previously contracted.
-- This exclusion ... applies only for the period of time specifically authorized under applicable State or Federal law or regulation
-- or, in the absence of such law or regulation, for a period of two years ..."
-- The period is stated, not computed: within it the company is excluded, after it the company is an affiliate again.
`f dpc within` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (dpcin "C")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "C" "Common" 30))
`f dpc expired` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (dpcexp "C")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "C" "Common" 30))
`f dpc none` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "C" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f dpc within` "C")
#ASSERT `aff A` `f dpc expired` "C"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f dpc none` "C"

§ `223.2(c) Subpart F: depository institutions are not affiliates`

-- "For purposes of subpart F (implementing section 23B), 'affiliate' with respect to a member bank also does not include any depository institution."
`f c di sibling` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (depinst "D1")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "D1" "Common" 30))
`f c plain sibling` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "C" "Common" 30))
`f c di parent` MEANS held (LIST (depinst "P")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30))
`f c fs sibling` MEANS held (LIST (finsub "Fsub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Fsub" "Common" 60))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f c di sibling` "D1"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff F` `f c di sibling` "D1")
-- the parent of the sibling is not a depository institution
#ASSERT `aff F` `f c di sibling` "P"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f c plain sibling` "C"
#ASSERT `aff F` `f c plain sibling` "C"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f c di parent` "P"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff F` `f c di parent` "P")
-- a depository institution subsidiary: an affiliate for 23A (a)(7), not for 23B
#ASSERT `aff A` `f di subsidiary` "Dsub"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff F` `f di subsidiary` "Dsub")
-- a financial subsidiary that is not a depository institution is an affiliate for both
#ASSERT `aff A` `f c fs sibling` "Fsub"
#ASSERT `aff F` `f c fs sibling` "Fsub"
-- through the step function
#ASSERT `step A` `f di subsidiary` EMPTY (depinst "Dsub")
#ASSERT NOT (`step F` `f di subsidiary` EMPTY (depinst "Dsub"))

§ `The list of affiliates and the one-at-a-time question agree`

-- One composite world.  Who is an affiliate, from the prongs and exclusions above:
--   P       parent (30 percent of the member bank)                            (a)(1)
--   Sis     30 percent held by P                                              (a)(2)
--   Co3     30 percent held by Ind, who holds 30 percent of the member bank   (a)(3)
--   Spon    sponsored by the member bank                                      (a)(5)
--   Pn      partnership of which the member bank is general partner           (a)(10)
--   SubDI   depository institution, 60 percent held by the member bank       (a)(7)   (not for 23B: (c))
--   SubFS   financial subsidiary, 60 percent held by the member bank         (a)(8)
--   Detm    determined by the Board                                           (a)(12)
--   SponSub 30 percent held by Spon, which is described in (a)(5)             (a)(11)
-- Not affiliates: Ind (an individual, not a company), Stranger (unconnected), Prem (30 percent held by P but engaged solely in holding the premises).
`f world` MEANS `full structure` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "Sis"), (indiv "Ind"), (corp "Co3"), (corp "Spon"), (pship "Pn"), (depinst "SubDI"), (finsub "SubFS"), (corp "Stranger"), (premco "Prem"), (corp "Detm"), (corp "SponSub")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "Ind" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "Sis" "Common" 30), (vote "Ind" "Co3" "Common" 30), (vote "Bank" "SubDI" "Common" 60), (vote "Bank" "SubFS" "Common" 60), (vote "P" "Prem" "Common" 30), (vote "Spon" "SponSub" "Common" 30)) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (LIST (lk "Bank" "Spon")) (LIST (lk "Bank" "Pn")) (LIST "Detm") EMPTY
#ASSERT `t same names` (`names A` `f world`) (LIST "P", "Sis", "Co3", "Spon", "Pn", "SubDI", "SubFS", "Detm", "SponSub")
#ASSERT `t same names` (`names F` `f world`) (LIST "P", "Sis", "Co3", "Spon", "Pn", "SubFS", "Detm", "SponSub")
#ASSERT `t consistent` `f world` `base readings` `Section 23A` (`t names` `f world`)
#ASSERT `t consistent` `f world` `base readings` `Subpart F, section 23B` (`t names` `f world`)

§ `Structures with cross-holdings`

-- Two companies, each holding 30 percent of the other, unconnected with the member bank: control runs both ways and nobody is an affiliate.
`f cross pair` MEANS held (LIST (corp "A"), (corp "B")) (LIST (vote "A" "B" "Common" 30), (vote "B" "A" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f cross pair` "A" "B"
#ASSERT controls `f cross pair` "B" "A"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f cross pair` "A")
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f cross pair` "B")
#ASSERT `t count` (`names A` `f cross pair`) EQUALS 0

-- A ring of three: X controls Y, Y controls Z, Z controls X; nothing connects the ring to the member bank.
`f cross ring` MEANS held (LIST (corp "X"), (corp "Y"), (corp "Z")) (LIST (vote "X" "Y" "Common" 30), (vote "Y" "Z" "Common" 30), (vote "Z" "X" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f cross ring` "X" "Z"
#ASSERT controls `f cross ring` "Z" "Y"
#ASSERT `t count` (`names A` `f cross ring`) EQUALS 0

-- A cross-holding below a parent: P controls S1, and S1 and S2 each hold 30 percent of the other.
`f cross under a parent` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S1"), (corp "S2")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "P" "S1" "Common" 30), (vote "S1" "S2" "Common" 30), (vote "S2" "S1" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f cross under a parent` "P" "S2"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f cross under a parent` "S1"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f cross under a parent` "S2"
#ASSERT `t same names` (`names A` `f cross under a parent`) (LIST "P", "S1", "S2")
#ASSERT `t consistent` `f cross under a parent` `base readings` `Section 23A` (`t names` `f cross under a parent`)

-- A cross-holding that includes the controlling shareholder: the shareholder and C each hold 30 percent of the member bank and
-- the shareholder holds 30 percent of C.
`f cross with shareholder` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "C")) (LIST (vote "I" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "I" "C" "Common" 30), (vote "C" "Bank" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f cross with shareholder` "C"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f cross with shareholder` "I")

§ `Affiliate step: the self-referential parts of 223.2`

-- `affiliate step` takes the names already found to be affiliates and asks whether 223.2 makes one more party an affiliate.
-- (a)(5): a company sponsored and advised by an affiliate of the member bank
-- Bank sponsors C1; C1 sponsors C2; C3 is unconnected.
`f step sponsored chain` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (corp "C1"), (corp "C2"), (corp "C3")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "Bank" "C1"), (lk "C1" "C2"))
#ASSERT `step A` `f step sponsored chain` EMPTY (corp "C1")
#ASSERT NOT (`step A` `f step sponsored chain` EMPTY (corp "C2"))
#ASSERT `step A` `f step sponsored chain` (LIST "C1") (corp "C2")
#ASSERT NOT (`step A` `f step sponsored chain` (LIST "C3") (corp "C2"))
#ASSERT NOT (`step A` `f step sponsored chain` (LIST "C1") (corp "C3"))
-- (a)(10): a partnership for which an affiliate serves as general partner
`f step partnership` MEANS `with general partners` (LIST (corp "A"), (pship "Pn")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "A" "Pn"))
#ASSERT NOT (`step A` `f step partnership` EMPTY (pship "Pn"))
#ASSERT `step A` `f step partnership` (LIST "A") (pship "Pn")
-- (a)(11): a subsidiary of an affiliate (the chaining reading of prong 11: any name already found)
#ASSERT NOT (`step A as` `chain readings` `f subsidiary of a sponsored company` EMPTY (corp "D1"))
#ASSERT `step A as` `chain readings` `f subsidiary of a sponsored company` (LIST "C1") (corp "D1")

§ `Contested readings`

-- Each assertion in this section depends on a point where the text can fairly be read two ways.
-- independent-readings.md gives, for each, the words that fork, the reading taken here and what the other reading would give.
-- The Readings constructors are explicit: an assertion made under the other constructor says what that reading must give.

-- R1  The member bank as its own affiliate: 223.2(a)(2) with 223.3(f).
--     "Any company, including any subsidiary of the member bank, that is controlled by a company that controls the member bank":
--     the member bank is a company and is controlled by P, which controls the member bank.
--     Taken: the member bank is not its own affiliate.  The literal reading says it is.
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f p30` "Bank")
#ASSERT `aff A as` `literal self readings` `f p30` "Bank"
#ASSERT `aff A as` `literal self readings` `f p30` "P"
#ASSERT `t same names` (`affiliates of the member bank` `f p30` `literal self readings` `Section 23A`) (LIST "P", "Bank")
-- a member bank is a depository institution, so under subpart F the literal reading still removes it: 223.2(c)
#ASSERT NOT (`aff F as` `literal self readings` `f p30` "Bank")
-- in the composite world of section `The list of affiliates and the one-at-a-time question agree`, where P controls the member bank
#ASSERT NOT (`t has` (`names A` `f world`) "Bank")
-- through the step function, however many affiliates are already known
#ASSERT NOT (`step A` `f p30` (LIST "P") `the bank`)
-- the same question under (a)(4): the member bank's own directors are a majority of the member bank's own board
`f bank board` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (indiv "d1"), (indiv "d2"), (indiv "d3")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "d1" "Bank"), (lk "d2" "Bank"), (lk "d3" "Bank"))
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f bank board` "Bank")
#ASSERT `aff A as` `literal self readings` `f bank board` "Bank"

-- R2  Interlocking directorates: "a majority of the persons holding any such office with the member bank or any company that controls the member bank".
--     Taken: one board at a time (the member bank, or one controlling company).  The other reading pools the offices.
--     b1..b3 sit on the member bank, p1..p3 on its parent P; Co has b1, b2, p1, p2 and e1.
--     Co's majority (3 of 5) is not a majority of either board alone (2 of 3 each, but 2 of 5 of Co's directors on each),
--     and is 4 of the 6 persons pooled.
`f il pooled` MEANS `with offices` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "Co"), (indiv "b1"), (indiv "b2"), (indiv "b3"), (indiv "p1"), (indiv "p2"), (indiv "p3"), (indiv "e1")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "b1" "Bank"), (lk "b2" "Bank"), (lk "b3" "Bank"), (lk "p1" "P"), (lk "p2" "P"), (lk "p3" "P"), (lk "b1" "Co"), (lk "b2" "Co"), (lk "p1" "Co"), (lk "p2" "Co"), (lk "e1" "Co"))
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f il pooled` "Co")
#ASSERT `aff A as` `pooled readings` `f il pooled` "Co"
-- pooling makes the bar higher in the other fixture: p1, p2 of Co's three are 2 of the 6 persons pooled
#ASSERT `aff A` `f il parent board` "Co"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A as` `pooled readings` `f il parent board` "Co")

-- R3  "directly controlled by": 223.3(g) does not define "directly".
--     P controls the member bank, which holds 60 percent of Sub.  P itself holds nothing in Sub.
--     Taken: direct control is the controller's own holdings, elections and determinations, so Sub is excluded as a subsidiary.
--     The other reading counts securities attributed from subsidiaries, so P directly controls Sub and Sub is an affiliate.
`f direct reading` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "Sub")) (LIST (vote "P" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "Bank" "Sub" "Common" 60))
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f direct reading` "Sub")
#ASSERT `aff A as` `any control readings` `f direct reading` "Sub"
#ASSERT controls `f direct reading` "P" "Sub"
#ASSERT NOT (`directly controls` `f direct reading` "P" "Sub")

-- R4  Prong (11): "Any subsidiary of a company described in paragraphs (a)(1) through (10)" and the heading "Subsidiaries of affiliates".
--     Taken: the body of the text: a subsidiary of a company DESCRIBED in (1) to (10), even if (b) then excludes that company.
--     The other reading: a subsidiary of an AFFILIATE, after the exclusions, and so chaining.
--     Prem is sponsored by the member bank, described in (a)(5) but excluded by (b)(2); it holds 30 percent of Dd.
`f prong eleven premises` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (premco "Prem"), (corp "Dd")) (LIST (vote "Prem" "Dd" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "Prem"))
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f prong eleven premises` "Prem")
#ASSERT `aff A` `f prong eleven premises` "Dd"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A as` `chain readings` `f prong eleven premises` "Dd")
-- the same with 223.2(c): a depository institution sponsored by the member bank, and its 30 percent company, under section 23B
`f prong eleven di` MEANS `with sponsorships` (LIST (depinst "D1"), (corp "Dd")) (LIST (vote "D1" "Dd" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "Bank" "D1"))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f prong eleven di` "D1"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff F` `f prong eleven di` "D1")
#ASSERT `aff A` `f prong eleven di` "Dd"
#ASSERT `aff F` `f prong eleven di` "Dd"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff F as` `chain readings` `f prong eleven di` "Dd")
-- a company determined under (a)(12) is not described in paragraphs (a)(1) through (10), so its subsidiary is not caught by the taken reading,
-- though Det is an affiliate (it is determined) and the subsidiary of an affiliate is caught by the chaining reading
#ASSERT `aff A` `f determined company` "Det"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f subsidiary of a determined company` "DS")
#ASSERT `aff A as` `chain readings` `f subsidiary of a determined company` "DS"
-- both readings agree where the chain is of holdings (223.3(g)(3) makes the grandchild a subsidiary of the first company)
#ASSERT `aff A as` `chain readings` `f subsidiary of a subsidiary` "E1"
-- through elections: depends on R7 as well; both readings say yes if control by election passes up through a subsidiary
`f prong eleven elections` MEANS `full structure` (LIST (corp "C1"), (corp "D1"), (corp "E1")) EMPTY (LIST (lk "C1" "D1"), (lk "D1" "E1")) EMPTY EMPTY (LIST (lk "Bank" "C1")) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY
#ASSERT `aff A` `f prong eleven elections` "D1"
#ASSERT `aff A as` `chain readings` `f prong eleven elections` "E1"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f prong eleven elections` "E1"

-- R5  Shares held as fiduciary and shares held on its own account, of one class: 223.3(g)(2) "by virtue of".
--     P holds 10 percent on its own account and 20 percent as fiduciary of the same class.
--     Taken: the fiduciary shares are disregarded, so 10 percent: no control.  The other reading adds them: 30 percent.
`f fiduciary mixed` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "Common" 10), (fiduciary "P" "T" "Common" 20))
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f fiduciary mixed` "P" "T")

-- R6  An individual who controls a company that holds securities: 223.3(g)(3) says "A company controls ... by any subsidiary".
--     Taken: the individual controls them too, by "directly or indirectly" in (g)(1)(i).  The other reading stops at companies.
`f individual through a company` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "I" "S" "Common" 30), (vote "S" "T" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f individual through a company` "I" "S"
#ASSERT controls `f individual through a company` "I" "T"

-- R7  Control by election through a subsidiary: 223.3(g)(3) attributes "securities, assets, or other ownership interests",
--     and (g)(1)(ii) says "controls in any manner the election".
--     P controls S; S controls the election of T's directors.  Taken: P controls T.  The other reading: P does not.
`f election through a subsidiary` MEANS `with elections` (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "S"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "S" "Common" 30)) (LIST (lk "S" "T"))
#ASSERT controls `f election through a subsidiary` "S" "T"
#ASSERT controls `f election through a subsidiary` "P" "T"

-- R8  Kinds of party that are persons but are not listed in 223.3(f): joint venture, pool, syndicate, unincorporated organization,
--     any other form of entity.  223.3(bb) lists them next to "company", not inside it.
--     Taken: not companies.  The other reading treats an unincorporated organization or a syndicate as an "association, or similar organization".
#ASSERT NOT (`kind is a company` `Joint venture`)
#ASSERT NOT (`kind is a company` Pool)
#ASSERT NOT (`kind is a company` Syndicate)
#ASSERT NOT (`kind is a company` `Unincorporated organization`)
#ASSERT NOT (`kind is a company` `Other form of entity`)

-- R9  A party flagged a depository institution whose kind is not on the (f) list: "includes ... a depository institution".
--     Taken: it is a company (the flag decides).  The other reading lets the kind decide.
#ASSERT `is a company` (held (LIST (Party OF "X", `Other form of entity`, TRUE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE)) EMPTY) (Party OF "X", `Other form of entity`, TRUE, FALSE, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE)

-- R10 A company that controls the member bank and is also its subsidiary (a cross-holding that includes the member bank).
--     A holds 30 percent of the member bank and the member bank holds 30 percent of A.
--     Taken, on the literal words: A is a subsidiary of the member bank, and 223.2(b)(1) excludes any subsidiary unless (i) to (v), none of which applies.
--     The other reading: A is a parent under (a)(1) and the exclusion was never meant to reach it.
`f cross with the bank` MEANS held (LIST (corp "A")) (LIST (vote "A" "Bank" "Common" 30), (vote "Bank" "A" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f cross with the bank` "A" "Bank"
#ASSERT controls `f cross with the bank` "Bank" "A"
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f cross with the bank` "A")

-- R11 A party flagged a financial subsidiary that the member bank does not control: 223.2(a)(8) "A financial subsidiary of the member bank".
--     Taken: not a subsidiary of the member bank, so not its financial subsidiary, so not an affiliate under (a)(8).
`f flagged but not held` MEANS held (LIST (finsub "Fsub")) (LIST (vote "Bank" "Fsub" "Common" 10))
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f flagged but not held` "Fsub")

-- R12 A determination under (a)(12) that names a party that is not a company: "Any company that the Board determines".
--     Taken: not an affiliate.  The other reading lets the determination decide.
#ASSERT NOT (`aff A` `f determined individual` "I")

-- R14 Fiduciary shares held by someone who is not a company: 223.3(g)(2) says "no company will be deemed to control".
--     An individual or a plain (non-business) trust holding 30 percent as fiduciary is not a "company" under 223.3(f).
--     Taken: the sentence is addressed to companies, so an individual or plain trust that holds 30 percent controls (223.3(g)(1): "company or shareholder").
--     The other reading applies the fiduciary exclusion to every holder: no control.
`f fiduciary plain trust` MEANS held (LIST (`party of kind` "P" Trust), (corp "T")) (LIST (fiduciary "P" "T" "Common" 30))
`f fiduciary individual holder` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "T")) (LIST (fiduciary "I" "T" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT controls `f fiduciary plain trust` "P" "T"
#ASSERT controls `f fiduciary individual holder` "I" "T"

-- R15 A list of control links that is not closed.
--     (a) 223.3(ii): C is controlled by B, and B by A, but the link (A, C) is not in the list.
--     Taken: the list is read as it stands, so C is not shown to be A's subsidiary.  The other reading closes the list under attribution.
#ASSERT NOT (`is a subsidiary of` `rel chain` "A" "C")
--     (b) `control step`: S2 holds 30 percent of T, S1 controls S2 and P controls S1, but (P, S2) is not in the list.
--     Taken: P reaches S2's shares, because 223.3(g)(3) says "owned or controlled, directly or indirectly, by any subsidiary" and the structure is at hand.
--     The other reading: the step looks only at the subsidiaries of P that the list names, so S2's shares are not attributed.
#ASSERT `control step` `f step two levels` (LIST (lk "P" "S1"), (lk "S1" "S2")) "P" "T"

-- R16 The exception in 223.3(g)(2): "except as provided in paragraph (a)(3) of § 223.2".
--     223.2(a)(3) reaches a company controlled "by trust or otherwise, by or for the benefit of shareholders who ... control ... the member bank".
--     Taken: a controlling shareholder of the member bank, individual or company, that holds shares of Co as fiduciary makes Co an affiliate,
--     reading "by ... shareholders" as the shareholder acting as trustee.  The other reading: the exception needs shares held "for the benefit of" such
--     shareholders by someone else, which the inputs cannot say, so the fiduciary holder's own control is excluded and Co is not an affiliate.
`f fiduciary individual` MEANS held (LIST (indiv "I"), (corp "Co")) (LIST (vote "I" "Bank" "Common" 30), (fiduciary "I" "Co" "Common" 30))
`f fiduciary corporate trustee` MEANS held (LIST (corp "TC"), (corp "Co")) (LIST (vote "TC" "Bank" "Common" 30), (fiduciary "TC" "Co" "Common" 30))
#ASSERT `aff A` `f fiduciary individual` "Co"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f fiduciary corporate trustee` "Co"
#ASSERT `aff A` `f fiduciary corporate trustee` "TC"

-- R13 Two rows of one holder and one class: the holder owns the sum.  (An input convention, not a reading of the text.)
`f split rows` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "Common" 15), (vote "P" "T" "Common" 10))
`f split rows classes` MEANS held (LIST (corp "P"), (corp "T")) (LIST (vote "P" "T" "A" 15), (vote "P" "T" "B" 10))
#ASSERT controls `f split rows` "P" "T"
#ASSERT NOT (controls `f split rows classes` "P" "T")

